{
  "schema": "table-tools-v1",
  "note": "The tool registry (D-681 item 7, scripts/tool_registry.py). Each entry is one tool a judge may ask Python to run in the one table tool request (scripts/table_tools.py), declared in one standard form. Product rule (D-694 item 3 a): when Shimmer runs as a product, no tool sends anything to the internet (no web search, no lookup, not even a masked or anonymised query); a tool computes only on what is already inside Shimmer's own run. Only the operator adds a tool; each is vetted by tools/vet_table_tool.py (license on the allowlist below, no socket, no file written, the same output in two fresh processes with different hash seeds, every example passing), which writes `vetting`. Boot refuses an entry whose vetting digest does not match its declaration and source module, or whose `approved_by` is not on `approving_decisions` (the operator's decisions that approve tools: D-681 fixes get_cells, difference and ratio; D-689 records the design and its defaults, which add find_figure, compare and column_extreme; D-694 item 4 approves the tools the tool audit adds, docs/loop/stages/TOOL_AUDIT.md: figure_step, rounds_to, percent_change, sum_cells, mean_cells and rank_in_column, in scripts/table_tools_extra.py, vetted by the building lane lane/tool-audit). The shipped vetting digests were written by the building lane (lane/table-tool); the operator path re-vets them before the request is switched on. Nothing here is read unless a judge contract declares request_tools under a ratified amendment.",
  "license_allowlist": [
    "MIT"
  ],
  "approving_decisions": [
    "D-681",
    "D-689",
    "D-694"
  ],
